& [CoreConclusion] is conditionally supported
  + a stable-identity graph and complete candidate-admission boundary can implement the common structural primitive of Honesty and Security
  + it completely fulfills those faculty purposes only when recognition includes grounding, admissibility, consequence, uncertainty, and independent faculty judgments
  + a digest and signature prove artifact identity, provenance claims, and recognized authority under a trust policy; they do not independently prove semantic truth, correct real-world binding, harmlessness, or safe use
  = concise: recognized identity establishes continuity while Honesty and Security establish whether the claimed binding and proposed use may be admitted

& [GraphDelineation] rejects one universal DAG without rejecting the DAG intuition
  + [semantic_relation_graph] is a typed directed property graph and may contain legitimate cycles, inverse edges, symmetric relations, and reentry
  + [derivation_graph] should be acyclic because a proof or derived artifact cannot be its own ancestor
  + [revision_graph] should be acyclic and append-only because each immutable revision cites prior identity state
  + [admission_graph] should be acyclic within one decision because candidate proof must precede admission
  + [authority_delegation_graph] should prohibit unauthorized cycles and confused-deputy transfer even when the wider relation graph cycles
  + [execution_trace] is ordinal and append-only within a cycle while repeated faculty cycles form a larger temporal recurrence
  = candidate: Cantor is one typed graph fabric with explicitly acyclic projections rather than one globally acyclic graph

& [IdentityBasin] is a coherent bounded identity neighborhood
  + [stable_key] is the durable identity coordinate
  + [immutable_revision] is the exact versioned declaration currently under judgment
  + [grounding_set] is observation, evidence, source, provenance, contract, and authority support
  + [invariant_set] is the meaning, attribution, status, purpose, scope, constraint, and effect properties that define continuity for the bounded purpose
  + [typed_edge_set] preserves direction, evidence, conditions, transfer law, non-transfer set, and invalidation
  + [proof_set] binds recognized bytes, source anchors, judgments, and admission or revocation state
  + [uncertainty_set] preserves inaccessible, disputed, unresolved, stale, and below-resolution material
  = must: derive basin strength from grounded coherence and invariant preservation rather than edge density, correlation weight, or self-consistency alone

& [StableIdentityBoundary] separates key continuity from changing state
  + a stable key must not contain fields that legitimately vary over time
  + changed definitions become new immutable revisions linked to the stable key
  + changed runtime conditions become new immutable snapshots or observations
  + a proposed transition is sandboxed until judged; an admitted after-snapshot can then become stable evidence without rewriting its predecessor
  - never: equate stable identity with permanently frozen state
  - never: mutate an admitted object in place while retaining its old digest or identity claim

& [IdentityRecognitionLayer] is a semantic reference monitor candidate
  + [complete_mediation] every node, edge, property transfer, revision, admission, query projection, and effect-relevant use crosses the recognition boundary
  + [tamper_evidence] admitted material is digest-bound, signature-checked, source-anchored, lifecycle-checked, and independently revalidated
  + [fail_closed] malformed, stale, revoked, unsigned, wrongly scoped, ambiguously bound, or incompletely judged material does not become admitted authority
  + [small_trusted_core] recognition and promotion rules remain deterministic, inspectable, bounded, and separable from learned routing
  + [non_bypass] correlation, model fluency, tool output, faculty consensus, or prior admission cannot bypass a current mandatory gate
  + [least_authority] recognition grants only the exact identity, relation, scope, and operation proved

& [CandidateSandbox] is logical quarantine with threat-model-dependent physical isolation
  + every unstable candidate receives a distinct content identity and explicit candidate lifecycle
  + candidate claims may cite admitted identities but cannot impersonate, mutate, supersede, or confer authority upon them
  + candidate edges are excluded from admitted traversal and inference unless a query explicitly requests candidate inspection
  + candidates have no effect authority and no implicit property, evidence, constraint, or authority transfer
  + resource, time, recursion, traversal, disclosure, and retention budgets bound inspection
  + inspection preserves candidate source, claimed identity, proposed delta, counterevidence, uncertainty, and faults
  + adversarial code, tools, files, or physical effects additionally require an operating-system or process sandbox; graph status alone is not physical isolation

& [PromotionProtocol] never changes candidate status in place without proof
  * unrecognized input -> content-addressed candidate
  * content-addressed candidate -> bounded candidate inspection
  * bounded candidate inspection -> Honesty and Security returns
  * Honesty and Security returns -> Observer disposition
  * Observer admit -> new immutable admitted revision plus proof and reentry record
  * Observer revise, decompose, block, or escalate -> candidate remains non-authoritative or produces a new candidate
  + supersession and revocation are new lifecycle records rather than deletion or history rewriting
  + promotion never imports unreviewed outgoing edges or hidden authority from the candidate

& [HonestyDuty] grounds claimed identity
  + verify that the candidate's claimed subject, meaning, relation, attribution, source, epistemic status, confidence, context, and delta correspond to admitted evidence at the declared resolution
  + detect a coherent basin built around the wrong referent, false premise, unsupported equivalence, omitted qualifier, or misattributed source
  + preserve unknown when evidence cannot decide the binding
  = counterexample: an immutable signed false clause has stable artifact identity but does not thereby have truthful semantic identity

& [SecurityDuty] grounds admissible identity use
  + verify that principal, mandate, authority, capability, protected subject, operation, scope, constraints, disclosure, and effect envelope remain valid across the candidate transition
  + prevent sandbox escape, authority laundering, property transfer, scope escalation, constraint erosion, and effect amplification
  + preserve unresolved risk when consequence bounds cannot be established
  = counterexample: an immutable signed dangerous instruction may be authentically recognized while its execution remains unsafe or prohibited

& [ObserverDuty] owns admission without collapsing independent gates
  + reconcile the identity frame, proposed delta, Honesty return, Security return, proof, counterevidence, and residual uncertainty
  + admit only a new immutable revision or snapshot whose exact content and relations were judged
  + one faculty cannot waive the other's material objection
  + recognition does not self-authorize admission merely because all bytes are internally consistent

& [CurrentImplementationFit] is partial and favorable
  + current compiled packages, recognition certificates, trust admission, immutable SemanticFabric, exact indexes, source anchors, query boundary accounts, candidate projections, and FacultyReturn statuses provide substantial substrate
  + current IdentityBoundary is static, singularly guarded, and lacks before frame, after frame, delta, invariant set, transition, and promotion proof
  + current ProjectionStatus distinguishes candidate material but does not define a general candidate-object quarantine or admission lifecycle
  + current trust admission recognizes compiled packages rather than arbitrary semantic-transition candidates
  + current implementation therefore demonstrates recognition mechanics but not the complete semantic reference monitor proposed here

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is IRDG-001 through IRDG-012
  + [IRDG-001] model Cantor as a typed graph fabric with explicitly declared acyclic projections
  + [IRDG-002] define IdentityBasin with stable key, immutable revision, grounding, invariants, typed edges, proof, and uncertainty
  + [IRDG-003] separate stable keys, immutable revisions, runtime snapshots, and proposed transitions
  + [IRDG-004] require complete mediation and fail-closed recognition for every admission-relevant node, edge, transfer, revision, and use
  + [IRDG-005] define candidate lifecycle, content identity, logical quarantine, budgets, and zero implicit authority
  + [IRDG-006] distinguish logical candidate quarantine from physical execution sandboxing
  + [IRDG-007] forbid candidate impersonation, in-place admitted mutation, unreviewed edge import, and authority transfer
  + [IRDG-008] require separate Honesty grounding and Security admissibility returns before Observer admission
  + [IRDG-009] promote by producing a new immutable admitted revision, proof bundle, lifecycle record, and reentry record
  + [IRDG-010] preserve rejected, blocked, unresolved, stale, superseded, and revoked identities without history rewriting
  + [IRDG-011] prove signatures establish artifact integrity and authority lineage without inflating them into truth or safety proof
  + [IRDG-012] test signed falsehood, signed unsafe instruction, wrong-referent basin, cyclic semantic relations, derivation cycle, sandbox escape, cumulative delta, legitimate revision, and unresolved evidence

& [Decision] is admit the architecture candidate into HSIBI preparation
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [signed_package_change] is none
  + [runtime_change] is none
  + [schedule_effect] expand HSIBI-SJS-01 to audit typed graph projections, identity basins, recognition limits, candidate quarantine, and promotion
  + [next] reconcile IRDG-001 through IRDG-012 with current trust, semantic fabric, FacultyCycle, SemanticTransition, truth-observation, commission, authority, and effect specifications
